&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Anthropic&#39;s Public Sector Sales Lead for France, you will be the face of Anthropic to the French State. This is a founding, zero-to-one role: there is no public sector team in France today, and you will build our strategy, our routes to market and our first strategic relationships from the ground up. Reporting to our EMEA South leadership, you will lead the adoption of safe, frontier AI across central government, starting with the largest ministries. You will work hand in hand with our Public Policy lead in Paris, because in few companies is policy as central to the mission as it is at Anthropic, and with Partnerships, Legal, Security and Product to put in place the commercial and compliance frameworks the State needs in order to work with us at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role. We expect you to have run a public sector business and led teams, and to be energised by stepping back into a hands-on seat where you build it yourself and where the size of your team says nothing about the size of your scope. In the first year, success is measured less by a large number and more by putting Anthropic on the map with the French State: a clear strategy, the right foundations and our first strategic agreements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own Anthropic&#39;s public sector go-to-market strategy for France: where we play first, how we win, and what we need to build to get there&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the senior face of Anthropic to the French State, building trusted relationships with ministerial cabinets, senior officials and digital and technology leaders across the largest ministries, including defence, finance and justice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle on our first strategic public sector opportunities, from first engagement through procurement route, close, deployment and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Partnerships, Legal and Finance to put in place the routes to market the State needs, including resale and partner channels, framework agreements and central purchasing bodies such as UGAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner day to day with our Public Policy lead in France so that commercial and policy engagement reinforce each other, and stay aligned with French and European AI strategy and regulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the conversation with customers on data sovereignty, security and compliance (for example SecNumCloud and the State&#39;s cloud doctrine), and work with Security, Legal and Product on how we meet those requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prove value with customers alongside a shared Applied AI architect, cloud providers and systems integrators, doing much of the groundwork yourself in the early stages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn from and contribute to our UK and US public sector teams, bringing what works to France and sharing what you learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create the playbooks, references and operating rhythm that will let us scale a public sector team in France over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years in enterprise technology sales, including significant time running a public sector business unit or leading sales teams that sell to French central government&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The appetite to move from a leadership role into a hands-on senior individual contributor role with no team at the outset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence that you thrive building from zero: a new market, a new business line or an early-stage company, where systems, processes and support were not yet in place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of landing large, complex and genuinely transformative agreements with major ministries, as the person leading the deal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep, senior network across central government, and the credibility to engage at director and cabinet level as well as with technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical command of French public procurement, including tenders, framework agreements, central purchasing bodies and partner or resale routes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real expertise in data sovereignty, security and compliance requirements in the French State, and experience leading those conversations with customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of, or a clear aptitude for, working closely with public policy or government affairs colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership and resilience: you treat what is missing as something to build, and you bring colleagues with you to build it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The technical curiosity to learn our products in depth and hold credible conversations with both engineering leaders and senior officials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French and English, with excellent written and spoken communication in both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to go through French security clearance (habilitation) should specific accounts require it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine commitment to safe and beneficial AI, and the ability to articulate why it matters for public institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;À propos du poste&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que Responsable des ventes secteur public d&#39;Anthropic pour la France, vous incarnerez Anthropic auprès de l&#39;État français. Il s&#39;agit d&#39;un poste fondateur, à construire de zéro : il n&#39;existe aujourd&#39;hui aucune équipe secteur public en France, et vous bâtirez notre stratégie, nos voies d&#39;accès au marché et nos premières relations stratégiques en partant d&#39;une page blanche. Ce poste est rattaché à la direction EMEA Sud. Vous piloterez l&#39;adoption d&#39;une IA de pointe et sûre au sein de l&#39;administration centrale, en commençant par les plus grands ministères. Vous travaillerez main dans la main avec notre responsable des affaires publiques à Paris — dans peu d&#39;entreprises les politiques publiques sont aussi centrales à la mission que chez Anthropic — ainsi qu&#39;avec les équipes Partenariats, Juridique, Sécurité et Produit, afin de mettre en place les cadres commerciaux et de conformité dont l&#39;État a besoin pour travailler avec nous à grande échelle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Il s&#39;agit d&#39;un poste senior de contribution individuelle. Nous attendons de vous que vous ayez dirigé une activité secteur public et encadré des équipes, et que la perspective de revenir à un poste pleinement opérationnel vous enthousiasme : un poste où vous construisez vous-même, et où la taille de votre équipe ne dit rien de l&#39;étendue de votre périmètre. La première année, la réussite se mesurera moins à un grand chiffre qu&#39;à votre capacité à installer Anthropic auprès de l&#39;État français : une stratégie claire, les bonnes fondations et nos premiers accords stratégiques.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsabilités&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Définir et porter la stratégie de mise sur le marché d&#39;Anthropic pour le secteur public en France : nos premiers terrains d&#39;action, nos leviers de succès et ce qu&#39;il nous faut construire pour y parvenir&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incarner Anthropic au plus haut niveau auprès de l&#39;État français, en nouant des relations de confiance avec les cabinets ministériels, les cadres dirigeants de l&#39;administration et les responsables du numérique et de la technologie des plus grands ministères, dont la défense, les finances et la justice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter l&#39;intégralité du cycle de vente sur nos premières opportunités stratégiques dans le secteur public, du premier contact au choix de la voie de passation, jusqu&#39;à la signature, au déploiement et à l&#39;extension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travailler avec les équipes Partenariats, Juridique et Finance pour mettre en place les voies d&#39;accès au marché dont l&#39;État a besoin : canaux de revente et de partenariat, accords-cadres et centrales d&#39;achat telles que l&#39;UGAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer au quotidien avec notre responsable des affaires publiques en France, pour que les démarches commerciales et politiques se renforcent mutuellement, en cohérence avec la stratégie et la réglementation française et européenne en matière d&#39;IA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mener les échanges clients sur la souveraineté des données, la sécurité et la conformité (par exemple SecNumCloud et la doctrine « cloud au centre »), et travailler avec les équipes Sécurité, Juridique et Produit sur la façon dont nous répondons à ces exigences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Démontrer la valeur auprès des clients en vous appuyant sur une expertise d&#39;architecture Applied AI mutualisée, sur les fournisseurs cloud et sur les intégrateurs, en réalisant vous-même une grande part du travail de terrain dans les premiers temps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apprendre de nos équipes secteur public au Royaume-Uni et aux États-Unis et contribuer à leur travail, en important en France ce qui fonctionne et en partageant vos enseignements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Créer les playbooks, les références clients et le rythme opérationnel qui nous permettront de faire grandir une équipe secteur public en France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ce poste peut vous correspondre si vous réunissez&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus de 15 ans dans la vente de technologies aux grandes organisations, dont une période significative à la tête d&#39;une activité secteur public ou à l&#39;encadrement d&#39;équipes commerciales à destination de l&#39;administration centrale française&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;L&#39;envie de passer d&#39;un poste d&#39;encadrement à un poste senior pleinement opérationnel, en contribution individuelle et sans équipe au départ&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un parcours qui montre que vous vous épanouissez en construisant à partir de zéro : un nouveau marché, une nouvelle ligne d&#39;activité ou une entreprise à ses débuts, là où les systèmes, les processus et les soutiens n&#39;existaient pas encore&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Des accords majeurs, complexes et réellement transformateurs conclus avec de grands ministères à votre actif, en étant la personne à la tête de la négociation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un réseau dense et de haut niveau au sein de l&#39;administration centrale, et la crédibilité nécessaire pour échanger au niveau des directions et des cabinets comme avec les équipes techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une maîtrise concrète de la commande publique française : appels d&#39;offres, accords-cadres, centrales d&#39;achat et voies de partenariat ou de revente&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une véritable expertise des exigences de souveraineté des données, de sécurité et de conformité au sein de l&#39;État français, et l&#39;expérience de ces échanges avec les clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;L&#39;expérience — ou une aptitude manifeste — du travail en étroite collaboration avec les équipes affaires publiques ou relations institutionnelles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Le sens de la responsabilité et la ténacité : ce qui manque est pour vous quelque chose à construire, et vous embarquez vos collègues dans cette construction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;La curiosité technique nécessaire pour apprendre nos produits en profondeur et tenir des échanges crédibles aussi bien avec les responsables d&#39;ingénierie qu&#39;avec les responsables publics de haut niveau&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un français et un anglais courants, avec une excellente expression écrite et orale dans les deux langues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;La disponibilité pour engager une procédure d&#39;habilitation de sécurité si certains comptes l&#39;exigent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un engagement sincère en faveur d&#39;une IA sûre et bénéfique, et la capacité d&#39;expliquer pourquoi cela compte pour les institutions publiques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€310.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€380.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you ----- addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Au sein de l&#39;équipe Content Moderation de Doctolib, vous jouez un rôle concret dans la fiabilité de notre plateforme. En veillant à la conformité des contenus publiés sur nos services, vous contribuez directement à maintenir la confiance de millions de patients et de professionnels de santé en Europe. Véritable bras droit de la manager, vous participez à la fois au bon fonctionnement quotidien de l&#39;équipe et à des projets stratégiques transverses — une expérience polyvalente, au cœur d&#39;un enjeu clé pour Doctolib.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vos missions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vos responsabilités incluent, mais ne sont pas limitées à :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participer à la modération du contenu au quotidien&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mettre à jour régulièrement les nouveautés de l’équipe sur l&#39;intranet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Réaliser une veille quotidienne sur les nouveaux actes, termes et pratiques à modérer sur les profils praticiens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Réaliser une veille réglementaire sur les sujets liés au droit d’exercer des soignants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rédiger des templates à faire relire par les équipes Legal en vue de missions de mise en conformité&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Les qualités attendues pour ce poste&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Avant de poursuivre votre lecture, si vous n&#39;avez pas le profil exact décrit ci-dessous, mais que vous pensez que cette description de poste correspond à vos compétences et à vos aspirations, nous vous encourageons tout de même à postuler.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous êtes étudiant(e) en Master (Bac+4/Bac+5) dans une école de commerce ou de communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous êtes organisé(e) et rigoureux(se), à l&#39;aise pour gérer plusieurs sujets en parallèle&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous avez de bonnes capacités rédactionnelles et de synthèse&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous aimez travailler en transversal avec différentes équipes et vous adapter à un environnement dynamique&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ce serait fantastique si :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous avez une formation complémentaire en droit, type bachelor en droit&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notre offre&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un programme d’onboarding complet, avec la Doctolib Academy et de nombreuses sessions de formation au sein de votre équipe (langues, soft skills, compétences techniques)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une carte Swile et de nombreuses offres de restauration au sein de nos locaux&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une offre de sport : un abonnement Urban Sports Club, des cours de sport gratuits dans les bureaux ou à distance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Le remboursement des titres de transport à 50%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;De nombreux bureaux offrant des espaces de collaboration et de bien-être&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une politique de travail flexible avec un mode hybride&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Le process de recrutement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un call RH avec Flore, Talent partner (15 minutes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entretien opérationnel avec restitution de cas pratique avec Sarah, Content Moderation Manager (1 heure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Détails du poste&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stage conventionné à temps plein&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Durée : 6 mois&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Début souhaité : Janvier 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lieu de travail : Levallois-Perret&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gratification: À définir selon niveau d’études&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chez Doctolib, nous sommes convaincus que nous devons améliorer la santé pour tout le monde. Cela se reflète dans notre processus de recrutement. Nous évaluons les candidatures uniquement sur la base des qualifications et de la motivation, sans aucune forme de discrimination.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Plus les idées sont diverses, plus notre produit améliorera véritablement la santé pour tout le monde. Vous pouvez postuler chez Doctolib, quel que soit votre genre, religion, âge, orientation sexuelle, origine ethnique ou handicap.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Afin de garantir l&#39;égalité des chances, nous vous invitons à exclure les informations personnelles (par exemple : photos, âge) de vos candidatures. Si vous avez besoin d&#39;aménagements particuliers, merci de nous en informer pour que nous puissions adapter le processus de recrutement. Rejoignez-nous pour construire la santé dont nous rêvons tous !&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;87&quot; data-end=&quot;122&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Toutes les informations fournies sont traitées par Doctolib pour la gestion des candidatures. Pour plus de détails sur le traitement des données, cliquez&lt;a href=&quot;https://doctolib.legal/B2C-Privacy-Policy-Career-FR&quot;&gt; ici&lt;/a&gt;. Veuillez contacter hr.dataprivacy(at)doctolib.com pour toute question ou pour exercer vos droits.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Soho House est un lieu encourageant la créativité sous toutes ses formes en permettant aux personnalités créatives de se rencontrer et de partager leurs idées. C’est une maison où les membres et les équipes se connectent, s’amusent et influencent.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous sommes à la recherche de notre futur(e) Stagiaire :&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Member Events&lt;/strong&gt; (H/F)&lt;br&gt;Le stagiaire chargé des événements sera responsable de la coordination et de l&#39;exécution de la programmation des événements pour les membres.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vos principales missions seront :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Promotion des évènements (mise en ligne de l’évènement, impression des affiches)&lt;br&gt;• Gestion des besoins des artistes (hébergement, accueil, hospitalité)&lt;br&gt;• Tâches administratives (organisation)&lt;br&gt;• Préparer les fiches de fonctions claires et détaillées pour chaque événement organisé par les membres. Les mettre à jour si nécessaire et s&#39;assurer que les détails de l&#39;événement (configuration de la salle, audiovisuel, exigences en matière de restauration, RVSP, liste d&#39;invités, etc.) sont correctement communiqués aux départements concernés. Si nécessaire, une formation au logiciel Opera ou Triple Seat sera apportée.&lt;br&gt;• Mettre à jour les détails des événements des membres sur la plateforme en ligne de Soho House et gérer les listes d&#39;attente.&lt;br&gt;• Assurer un suivi avec les partenaires de l&#39;événement afin de s&#39;assurer que toutes les informations nécessaires ont été collectées et être au courant des changements éventuels. Assurer le suivi avec les partenaires de l&#39;événement avant l&#39;événement afin de recueillir leurs commentaires.&lt;br&gt;• S&#39;occuper des transports en avion et des demandes d&#39;hébergement des partenaires des événements.&lt;br&gt;• Remplir les formulaires internes requis et veiller à ce que les départements internes concernés soient informés.&lt;br&gt;• Gérer une base de données d&#39;adhésions et déposer les demandes auprès de l&#39;équipe chargée de celles-ci.&lt;br&gt;• Aider le responsable des événements des membres à compiler les informations relatives aux événements des membres pour le calendrier du mois suivant.&lt;br&gt;• Proposer des idées créatives d&#39;événements aux responsables des secteurs de l&#39;art, de la mode, du divertissement, de la musique, du cinéma, de la gastronomie et de la technologie.&lt;br&gt;• Toutes autres tâches confiées par le Responsable des Events&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profil &amp;amp; Compétences :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Maîtrise d’Excel et de l’Anglais professionnel&lt;br&gt;• Vous êtes étudiant(e) en Bac +3 ou Master, de préférence dans le domaine de la gestion de la culture et des arts ou de la production et de la communication culturelles&lt;br&gt;• Soucis du détail, sens développé de l’organisation&lt;br&gt;• Un véritable intérêt pour les événements culturels, les médias et les arts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rémunération&lt;/strong&gt; : 708€ - un repas offert par jour de travail&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; Durée du stage&lt;/strong&gt; : 6 mois – 35h hebdo&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify is a product-led growth company, and Revenue Operations owns the systems, data, and infrastructure that turn that growth into revenue.&amp;nbsp; With a large volume of people discovering and signing up for Netlify every day, Marketing Operations is critical to understanding those users, connecting activity across our systems, and creating scalable ways to engage them throughout their journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Marketing Operations Manager, you’ll own the operational foundation behind that work. You’ll connect HubSpot, Salesforce, product data, and analytics, build the systems and lifecycle infrastructure that turn signals into action, and give Marketing and our GTM partners trusted visibility into performance. Reporting to the Senior Director of Revenue Operations, you’ll translate the Marketing Operations vision into a roadmap and independently drive it forward while partnering closely with Growth, RevOps, Data, Product, and other GTM teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute on the Marketing Operations roadmap, translating broader Marketing and GTM priorities into scalable systems, processes, and programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our marketing automation platform end to end, including workflows, lifecycle stages, segmentation, forms, lists, email operations, data hygiene, deliverability, governance, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the connection between marketing automation, Salesforce, product data, and analytics so we can understand and engage users throughout the customer journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish reliable attribution and measurement across marketing and product-led journeys, including UTM governance and connections between campaigns, signups, activation, conversion, and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reporting and self-service dashboards that give Marketing and GTM partners a trusted view of performance and support weekly, monthly, and executive-level decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Growth to operationalize lifecycle programs across email, in-product experiences, and sales-assist triggers, turning customer and product signals into scalable journeys from signup through activation and conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build experimentation infrastructure that allows marketers to launch, measure, and learn from tests without requiring engineering support for every experiment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational health of the MarTech stack, including integrations, data flows, governance, vendor relationships, and periodic assessments of what we should keep, retire, consolidate, or integrate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish scalable practices for high-volume email operations, including audience management, domain and inbox health, deliverability, and safeguards that protect the customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn large and sometimes ambiguous datasets into actionable recommendations, identifying points of friction or drop-off and partnering with Marketing, Growth, Product, Data, and RevOps on opportunities to improve conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Marketing Operations portion of the broader Marketing budget and evaluate technology investments based on business value, scalability, and ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore emerging capabilities in AI-enabled marketing operations and AI visibility measurement, helping the team establish useful workflows and baselines as the space develops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in Marketing Operations or a closely related discipline, with experience operating independently in a complex B2B SaaS or product-led growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with marketing automation platforms and CRM systems such as HubSpot, Marketo, Eloqua, and Salesforce, including lifecycle stages, campaign architecture, attribution, lead or account routing, and data governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with high-volume customer or prospect datasets and designing segmentation, lifecycle, and operational approaches that remain reliable at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience operating high-volume email programs, with a practical understanding of deliverability, domain and inbox reputation, audience management, warming strategies, and the risks that emerge at large sending volumes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and the ability to investigate complex datasets, identify meaningful patterns, question the quality of the underlying data, and turn findings into recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating lifecycle, nurture, or in-product engagement programs tied to measurable activation or conversion outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems thinking and experience designing integrations across marketing automation, CRM, product, analytics, and data systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building measurement and experimentation infrastructure that enables other teams to operate and learn independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong GTM fluency and an understanding of how Marketing Operations, Growth, Sales, RevOps, Product, and Customer Success connect to customer experience and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using AI-enabled tools and workflows to accelerate your work while applying judgment to validate outputs and determine where automation is (and isn’t) appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with product analytics tools such as Amplitude and experience with emerging AEO or AI-visibility tooling is helpful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with contractors, agencies, or distributed partners is helpful but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with developer tools, web platforms, or another high-volume PLG business is useful, but we value relevant operating experience over category-specific expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role Is a Great Fit If&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy building the foundation, not just operating what someone else has already built. You’re energized by taking an imperfect system and creating something scalable, measurable, and trusted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable moving between architecture and execution. You can define how a system should work and then get into the details yourself when necessary to make it work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive with significant autonomy. Given a goal and context, you investigate the problem, weigh tradeoffs, make a recommendation, and drive the work forward without needing a detailed playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You genuinely enjoy data. Large, messy datasets make you curious, and you’re willing to dig until you understand what is happening and what the business should do about it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care deeply about operational quality. Data integrity, attribution, documentation, audience segmentation, and email deliverability aren’t afterthoughts—they’re part of building a trustworthy growth engine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You balance speed with judgment. You know when to move quickly, when a shortcut creates unacceptable downstream risk, and when to challenge an approach that won’t scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You see AI as a way to amplify good judgment and increase leverage rather than a substitute for understanding the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly in an async, distributed environment and can build alignment across Marketing, Growth, Product, Sales, RevOps, and Data without relying on organizational authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applying&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet 100% of our qualifications? &lt;strong&gt;Please apply anyway!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When applying please include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A resume or short listing of your job history &amp;amp; skills (link to a LinkedIn profile would be fine). We appreciate a cover letter explaining why you would enjoy working in this role at Netlify to get to know you a bit better, though this is not required and will not impact your application. Our mission is to “build a better web” and that cannot be done without a diversity of skill sets, backgrounds and thoughts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Of everything we&#39;ve ever built at Netlify, we are most proud of our team. Netlify is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are devoted to building a team of people with diverse backgrounds and lifestyles. Driving equality empowers our team, enables us to innovate, and helps us maintain a more inclusive environment. We don’t discriminate against employees or applicants based on gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, age, race, military/veteran status, citizenship, pregnancy status, or any other differences. If we can do anything to provide a better interview, i.e. accommodate a disability, then please let us know by emailing &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accomodations@netlify.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@netlify.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Netlify&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify is the most popular way to build, deploy, and scale modern web applications, empowering everyone from fast moving solo developers to enterprise teams. Millions of developers and organizations rely on Netlify as their platform of choice for composing web applications that are production ready, performant, and flexible. Now, as we embrace the next era of software development, we are embedding the same fluid, intuitive experience into the Agent Experience (AX), making it just as simple for intelligent agents to understand, interact with, and act on our platform as it is for developers. Whether your user is human or machine, Netlify ensures the path from idea to URL is seamless, fast, and deeply reliable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Series D company that has raised over $200M from investors such as Andreessen Horowitz, Kleiner Perkins, EQT, Bessemer, BOND, and Menlo Ventures. As a fully distributed company, we aim to create a company culture where the best idea can come from anywhere and strive to be thoughtful, compassionate, and collaborative in our work. If this sounds like something you’d like to be part of, we’re excited to connect with you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Netlify, we are committed to a compensation philosophy that prioritizes fairness and equity, positions our employee compensation competitively in the market, recognizes and rewards performance, and takes a comprehensive approach to our rewards package. We anchor our compensation philosophy on a market-based approach, therefore salary ranges may differ depending on the labor cost in a particular location. The salary provided is in addition to robust benefits and participation in Netlify’s equity plan. Our hiring range for this role is targeted at $155,000 - $210,000 for most US-based locations.&amp;nbsp; Candidates outside the US or in premium markets should consult with their Talent Acquisition partner regarding location-based ranges, as they may be higher or lower than the average US range listed. The starting pay will be determined based on multiple factors, including expertise and skills, market demands, experience, internal equity, and applicable geographic location. These compensation packages and ranges are subject to change and may be modified in the future.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify’s Finance team builds the financial foundation that helps the company plan, operate, and make informed decisions. The team owns our operating model, management reporting, budgeting and planning, and the company-level metrics leadership uses to understand performance and make tradeoffs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Finance Manager, you’ll own the core corporate finance cycle - from monthly reporting and forecasting to planning, scenario analysis, and KPI reporting - and help shape how those processes evolve as Netlify scales. This is a hands-on role with meaningful room to improve how the function operates: strengthening the models and insights behind business decisions while using AI, automation, and better tooling to make Finance faster, more scalable, and less dependent on manual work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the monthly reporting cadence: updating operating models, variance analysis, and the management reporting package, with actionable insights for leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take full responsibility for the 3-statement operating model and driver-based forecast, including structural changes to how the model is built as our business scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive the annual planning process, including planning templates, scenario models, and turning strategic priorities into the assumptions and targets the plan is built on&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the company-level KPI and metrics layer, including ARR, NRR, gross margin, CAC payback, and Rule of 40, and explain what moved and why each month&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the scenario and sensitivity models leadership uses to make capital and headcount decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own department-level budget tracking, and serve as the standing point of contact for department leaders on budget, headcount, and software spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate manual work across the close and forecast cycles using AI and better tooling, with measurable reduction in cycle time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to partner with GTM leadership on sales planning and KPI tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in FP&amp;amp;A or strategic finance, including several at a SaaS or usage-based business. An investment banking, consulting or private equity background preferred; but strong modeling skills, ability to develop frameworks to solve complex problems and ability to run scenarios is a must&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of building 3-statement models from scratch, with scenario and sensitivity analysis, and of making structural changes to a model rather than only updating inputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of US GAAP and core accounting principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Google Sheets or Excel, and comfort with large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep command of SaaS metrics and their drivers, with a point of view on which ones actually matter at our stage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how financial data flows and experience reconciling systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in ambiguity and defining your own approach to problems that arrive without a defined scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as the finance point of contact for non-finance leaders, and the ability to make financial concepts clear to people who don&#39;t speak finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building AI workflows for finance work, including validating AI output and understanding where AI fails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep curiosity about our business, product, customers, competitors and industry trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role Is a Great Fit If&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to own a function, not contribute to one. The monthly close, the operating model, and the planning cycle would be yours to run and to redesign.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable being the only person on this work. There is no junior analyst supporting the role and no plan to add one. You will build it and run it yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take quality seriously. You know the difference between a variance explanation that&#39;s technically accurate and one that&#39;s actually useful to a business leader, and you hold yourself to the latter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You notice when something is slower or more manual than it needs to be, and you fix it without being asked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You feel confident communicating directly with department leaders about budget and headcount.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re excited to build. The tooling, the reporting layer, and the automation work are all genuinely open, and there is room to make this function structurally better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applying&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet 100% of our qualifications? Please apply anyway!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When applying please include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A resume or short listing of your job history &amp;amp; skills (link to a LinkedIn profile would be fine). We appreciate a cover letter explaining why you would enjoy working in this role at Netlify to get to know you a bit better, though this is not required and will not impact your application. Our mission is to &quot;build a better web&quot; and that cannot be done without a diversity of skill sets, backgrounds and thoughts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Of everything we&#39;ve ever built at Netlify, we are most proud of our team. Netlify is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are devoted to building a team of people with diverse backgrounds and lifestyles. Driving equality empowers our team, enables us to innovate, and helps us maintain a more inclusive environment. We don&#39;t discriminate against employees or applicants based on gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, age, race, military/veteran status, citizenship, pregnancy status, or any other differences. If we can do anything to provide a better interview, i.e. accommodate a disability, then please let us know by emailing &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accommodations@netlify.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@netlify.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Netlify&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify is the most popular way to build, deploy, and scale modern web applications, empowering everyone from fast moving solo developers to enterprise teams. Millions of developers and organizations rely on Netlify as their platform of choice for composing web applications that are production ready, performant, and flexible. Now, as we embrace the next era of software development, we are embedding the same fluid, intuitive experience into the Agent Experience (AX), making it just as simple for intelligent agents to understand, interact with, and act on our platform as it is for developers. Whether your user is human or machine, Netlify ensures the path from idea to URL is seamless, fast, and deeply reliable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Series D company that has raised over $200M from investors such as Andreessen Horowitz, Kleiner Perkins, EQT, Bessemer, BOND, and Menlo Ventures. As a fully distributed company, we aim to create a company culture where the best idea can come from anywhere and strive to be thoughtful, compassionate, and collaborative in our work. If this sounds like something you&#39;d like to be part of, we&#39;re excited to connect with you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Netlify, we are committed to a compensation philosophy that prioritizes fairness and equity, positions our employee compensation competitively in the market, recognizes and rewards performance, and takes a comprehensive approach to our rewards package. We anchor our compensation philosophy on a market-based approach, therefore salary ranges may differ depending on the labor cost in a particular location. The salary provided is in addition to robust benefits and participation in Netlify&#39;s equity plan. Our hiring range for this role is targeted at $123,000 - $166,000 for most US-based locations. Candidates outside the US or in premium markets should consult with their Talent Acquisition partner regarding location-based ranges, as they may be higher or lower than the average US range listed. The starting pay will be determined based on multiple factors, including expertise and skills, market demands, experience, internal equity, and applicable geographic location. These compensation packages and ranges are subject to change and may be modified in the future.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Engagement Manager plays the critical role in helping Customers drive adoption of high value functionality of the GitLab platform. The Engagement Manager plays a sales overlay role by shaping customer engagements focused helping customers accelerated toward their positive business outcomes with GitLab. The Engagement Manager serves as a trusted advisor to customers in their portfolio, providing guidance to Sales, Customer Success and Professional Services Delivery team and ensuring the highest levels of customer satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform discovery (with account team or with customer) to understand customer current-state, constraints and desired positive business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;French language is essential for this position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify standard and custom services to align to customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build custom-scoped services engagement proposals for key strategic customers with guidance/review from Sr. Engagement Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain technical solution proposal to account team and/or customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet and exceed set financial targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain GitLab Services value proposition, catalog of service offerings, and methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain standard packaged solutions to Customer to gain agreement to move forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customer understand commercial terms - price, period of performance, payment/invoice structure, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide Account team to execute governing legal agreement to execute services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach Account Executives on how to include consulting and education services on quote/order form.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closing process with help from Account Executive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate staffing requirements with PS Operations team to ensure skillset, language, and timezone match are appropriate for each engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle standard objections related to price, DIY implementations, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update quarterly bookings forecast on a weekly basis using Salesforce/Clari.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and communicate risks to account executives and EM leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with Account Executives, Customer Success Managers and Solutions Architects within their patch to ensure Global Services are included as part of the standard customer journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join Sales leadership forecast calls (within patch) to report on Services Forecast and to identify key customer accounts where services should be attached.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide timely and predictable responses to incoming questions/requests from customers or account executives to reinforce positive brand of Global Services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish mentorship with more senior engagement manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setup individual development plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate trends in customer behavior to Practice Management team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
