&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Product Management: Agentic Software Delivery, you&#39;ll own one of GitLab&#39;s most strategic sections, spanning Continuous Integration, Artifact Management, Continuous Deployment, and Observability. You&#39;ll lead senior and principal product managers and be accountable for adoption, retention, and revenue across build, package, deploy, and monitor. Today, these are separate stages with a human making the call at each handoff. As agents take on more coding, pipeline, and deployment work, you&#39;ll set the three-year vision for how much of that judgment the system can make safely and how quickly a production signal can turn into a fix without waiting for a human to notice it first. You&#39;ll define how customers move from today&#39;s manual checkpoints toward agent-driven software delivery at a pace that fits their risk tolerance. In your first year, you&#39;ll bring four connected roadmaps into one coherent strategy, establish how investment is allocated and reallocated, deepen partnerships with Engineering and go-to-market leaders, and give customers a credible path for managing software delivery at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Own the strategy, three-year vision, and business outcomes for GitLab&#39;s Agentic Software Delivery section, with a clear point of view on how artificial intelligence is changing software delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Lead and develop senior and principal product managers across Continuous Integration, Artifact Management, Continuous Deployment, and Observability, helping them grow as independent decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Establish the frameworks, standards, and operating rhythm that support consistent, high-quality product decisions without unnecessary escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Own section-level key performance indicators and adoption funnels, using the results to reallocate investment or stop work that isn&#39;t paying off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Evaluate major strategic bets, partnerships, and build, buy, or partner decisions, and develop the business cases that support them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Partner with Engineering leadership on platform investment, architectural direction, and trade-offs across the section, while connecting build, package, deploy, and monitor into one coherent customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Drive pricing, packaging, go-to-market strategy, migration, and adoption with Product Marketing, Sales, Pricing, Customer Success, and Solutions Engineering across free, commercial, and enterprise offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Represent the section with GitLab&#39;s senior leadership, key enterprise customers, partners, and industry audiences, while modeling AI-native product management across discovery, synthesis, prototyping, roadmap exploration, and concept development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Experience leading product managers, including developing senior and principal talent, hiring, and addressing performance directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;A track record of owning a portfolio across multiple product areas and being accountable for adoption, retention, and revenue, not only roadmap delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Product management depth in one or more relevant areas, such as continuous integration and continuous delivery pipelines, artifact or package management, release management, or observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Sound judgment about where to invest and where to stop, including experience making and defending build, buy, or partner decisions with a business case.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Technical fluency to work with engineers and architects on pipeline design, artifact workflows, deployment strategies, and observability signals such as logs, metrics, and traces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Experience shaping pricing and packaging for technical products across free, commercial, and enterprise offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Experience working with technical customers in developer tools, DevOps, or software delivery environments where engineers and engineering leaders are primary users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Executive-level communication and influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;9&quot;&gt;Practical use of AI tools in product management workflows, along with a thoughtful view of how AI and agentic workflows are changing software delivery. We welcome candidates whose experience may come from different but transferable product and leadership paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team brings together senior product leaders across GitLab&#39;s software delivery platform and works closely with Engineering, Design, and go-to-market partners so customers experience these capabilities as one connected system. The team helps customers manage today&#39;s delivery complexity while shaping how AI-powered and AI-native workflows influence the next generation of software delivery. As part of GitLab&#39;s all-remote organization, the team collaborates asynchronously across regions with a focus on transparency, written communication, and clear decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&amp;nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role&#39;s base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&amp;nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&amp;nbsp;and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our &lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLBeneUS&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;